comment.narrative:
1. 4 Technical Assistance (TA) proposals approved for Gender, Green Economy, Capacity Building and Blue Economy. Implementation initiated for Gender, Green Economy and Blue Economy. Implementation for capacity building to start in 2021. The Millennium Institute TA was withdrawn.
2. 2020 marked the start of three new partnerships formed at regional level through Technical Assistance (TA);
• UN Women on increasing regional priorities and investments in environmentally and gender responsive Climate-Smart Agriculture https://pea4sdgs.org/ta-projects/gender-agriculture • Asia Development Bank (ADB) on Blue Economy focusing on identifying and developing Poverty-Environment Initiative (PEI) / Poverty-Environment Action tools that support budgeting and financing for a blue economy and disseminating this work through regional seas programmes and the Forum of Ministers and Environment Authorities of Asia Pacific https://pea4sdgs.org/ta-projects/blue-economy • GIZ on Green Bonds in South Africa building on Synergies between Low-emissions Pathways and the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). https://pea4sdgs.org/ta-projects/green-bonds . This has also enhanced South South Knowledge transfer and Corporation for Indonesia and South Africa.
